course: dictionary
lesson: 6857
title: Many meanings of over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word over has many meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Read the clues before you choose. «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish at over eight kilometres.» Here over means more than. Test it by swapping in «more than eight kilometres»: it still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: «Muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest.» Here over means during, because «months» shows time passing. Now look at «The game is over.» Here over means finished. It is the same little word, but the clues in each sentence show a different meaning.
explain: Over can also mean above or across, as in «the bird flew over the tree». When you meet over, try the meanings one at a time in the sentence. Ask yourself which meaning makes the sentence sensible, then keep that one.
fact: Over means above, or across from one side to the other, as in «the bird flew over the tree».
fact: Over means more than, as in «over 10», which means more than 10.
fact: Over means finished, as in «The game is over», and it can also mean again, as in «do it over».
fact: Over means during, as in «over the weekend», and it covers things, as in «a blanket over the bed».
fact: In cricket, an over is six balls bowled by one bowler.
exercise: «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish at over eight kilometres.» What does over mean here? | Finished | Covering | Above | *More than
exercise: «The game is over.» What does over mean here? | *Finished | Again | More than | Covering
exercise: «The bird flew over the tree.» Which meaning of over fits this sentence? | More than | Finished | Covering | *Above or across
test: «Writing was invented in China over 3,000 years ago.» What does over mean here? | Above | *More than | Finished | During
test: Mum says, «Let's do the puzzle over.» What does over mean here? | Covering | *Again | Above | Finished
exam: «Muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest.» What does over mean here? | Finished | More than | Above | *During
